OL,3,AKing and Macron arrive for sneak
OL,4,Apreview of landmark Bayeux Tapestry
OL,5,Aexhibition
OL,6,
OL,7,FKing Charles, French President Emmanuel
OL,8,FMacron and UK Prime Minister Andy
OL,9,FBurnham have arrived at the British
OL,10,FMuseum for a preview of the Bayeux
OL,11,FTapestry exhibition, which is set to be
OL,12,Fone of the blockbuster cultural events
OL,13,Fof the year.
OL,15,FThe visit on Wednesday evening comes
OL,16,Fahead of the medieval tapestry going on
OL,17,Fpublic display in London from 10
OL,18,FSeptember.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1788369856
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AKing and Macron arrive for sneak
OL,4,Apreview of landmark Bayeux Tapestry
OL,5,Aexhibition
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe 70m (230ft) tapestry, originally
OL,8,Fembroidered in England but kept for
OL,9,Fcenturies in France, tells the story of
OL,10,Fthe Norman Conquest and the Battle of
OL,11,FHastings in 1066.
OL,13,FPresident Macron said the loan of the
OL,14,Fnational treasure until July 2027 was a
OL,15,F"powerful symbol" of the close ties
OL,16,Fbetween the UK and France.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/19
